<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kalinyamat</h1><p class="st-meta">1549 CE – 1579 CE (approx.) · capital Kalinyamat (Jepara)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The north Javanese state of Ratu Kalinyamat, the warrior queen of Jepara who twice sent fleets against Portuguese Malacca.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kalinyamat, near the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jepara">Jepara</a>, was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-hadlirin">Sultan Hadlirin</a> and his wife, a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trenggana">Sultan Trenggana of Demak</a>. In 1549, during the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/demak-sultanate">Demak</a> succession war, Hadlirin was murdered by agents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arya-penangsang">Arya Penangsang</a>. His widow became ruler, remembered as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratu-kalinyamat">Ratu Kalinyamat</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratu-kalinyamat">Ratu Kalinyamat</a> helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadiwijaya">Hadiwijaya of Pajang</a> defeat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arya-penangsang">Arya Penangsang</a> and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jepara">Jepara</a> a leading port and shipbuilding centre. She sent fleets to support attacks on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-malacca">Portuguese Malacca</a> in 1551 and 1574, and Portuguese writers called her the queen of Japara. She also patronised mosques such as the one at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mantingan-mosque">Mantingan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratu-kalinyamat">Ratu Kalinyamat</a> died around 1579, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jepara">Jepara</a> came under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pajang-sultanate">Pajang</a> and then the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram Sultanate</a>. She was named a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-hero-of-indonesia">National Hero of Indonesia</a> in 2023.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kalinyamat.jpg" alt="Kalinyamat" width="320" height="186"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AMH_L%27isola_Giava_Maggiore_e_discoste_dall%27isola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1549 CE – 1579 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kalinyamat (Jepara)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sultan Hadlirin, Ratu Kalinyamat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Javanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Indonesia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jepara (Kalinyamat)</dd></dl></aside></div>
